Package: libzyphra-textnorm-tts
Architecture: amd64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: text normalization for TTS in 43 languages (private library)
 zyphra-textnorm turns written text into its spoken form ("$5.32" ->
 "five dollars thirty two cents", "am 3. Oktober" -> "am dritten
 Oktober") for 43 languages: Rust ports of the NeMo text processing
 grammars and Zyphra's locale grammars, with all tables built in.
 .
 This package has its C library in /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts for the
 speech-dispatcher modules of the linux-tts PPA, which load it for the
 voices of languages other than Russian.
